  "description": "Illustrates the value for a planet's bulk density.",
  "definition": "Measured in grams per cubic centimeter (g/cm\u00b3). Puffy gas giants can have densities less than water (<1 g/cm\u00b3), while dense, rocky planets like Earth have densities around 5.5 g/cm\u00b3."
}

