  "description": "Illustrates the value for the distance to a star system.",
  "definition": "Measured in parsecs (pc), where 1 parsec equals about 3.26 light-years. Values range from nearby stars like Proxima Centauri (~1.3 pc) to stars thousands of parsecs away."
}

